    {
      "id": "p0087-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Watashi is the most neutral version of \"I/me\" in Japanese. In formal situations, watashi can be used by almost anyone. In informal situations, watashi is a tad more feminine. Other fictional characters who use watashi include:",
        "raw": "Watashi is the most neutral version of \"I/me\" in Japanese. In formal situations,\nwatashi can be used by almost anyone. In informal situations, watashi is a\ntad more feminine. Other fictional characters who use watashi include:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.12512929,
          0.10973571,
          0.68176164,
          0.15652857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.12380893,
