    {
      "id": "p0087-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The main character starts with the \"Bandage\" item. In English, \"bandage\" can refer to either an adhesive bandage or a bandage wrap. This ambiguity was intentional, but late-game text suggests \"bandage wrap\" was intended.",
        "raw": "The main character starts with the \"Bandage\" item. In English, \"bandage\" can\nrefer to either an adhesive bandage or a bandage wrap. This ambiguity was\nintentional, but late-game text suggests \"bandage wrap\" was intended.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09722911,
          0.75233571,
          0.6963262,
          0.80163571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09519779,
          0.75162143,
          0.70682813,
          0.80270714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          26,
          27,
          28
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "主角开局就带着一件叫 Bandage（绷带）的物品。英语 bandage 既可以指创可贴，也可以指缠绕式绷带。这种歧义是刻意保留的，不过游戏后期的文本表明，它应该指缠绕式绷带。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09747795,
          0.75090714,
          0.70479681,
          0.80520714
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "font_weight": 450,
        "background": "transparent",
        "text_align": "justify",
        "auto_height": true,
        "limit_bottom": 0.9242857142857143,
        "snap_to_guides": true,
        "resize_anchor": "left"
      },
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.09747795,
          0.75090714,
          0.70479681,
          0.80520714
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 29.0
      },
      "review_issues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0087-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In Japanese, however, these two types of bandages go by different names: bans6k6 (\"adhesive bandage\") and h6tai (\"bandage wrap\"). Unfortunately, this language difference forced the translator to use h6tai, which removes the intended ambiguity and prevents Japanese players from experiencing the same confusion as English-speaking players.",
        "raw": "In Japanese, however, these two types of bandages go by different names:\nbans6k6 (\"adhesive bandage\") and h6tai (\"bandage wrap\"). Unfortunately, this\nlanguage difference forced the translator to use h6tai, which removes the\nintended ambiguity and prevents Japanese players from experiencing the same\nconfusion as English-speaking players.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09772679,
          0.81645,
          0.70479681,
          0.90285
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09519779,
          0.81573571,
          0.70682813,
          0.90392143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          29,
          30,
          31,
          34,
          35
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "但在日语中，两者有不同的名称：bansōkō（创可贴）与 hōtai（缠绕式绷带）。遗憾的是，这个语言差异迫使译者选择了 hōtai，也消除了原本有意留下的歧义，使日本玩家无法像英语玩家那样感到困惑。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
